From: A Link Between Dusklight (WW port lane)
Subject: [PATCH] gx: fix LOAD_INDX array selection and wire format

Two defects in the indexed-XF (LOAD_INDX) path of the FIFO parser. Both are
PLATFORM bugs, not content bugs: the opcode is emitted by core J3D
(J3DShapeMtx::loadMtxIndx_PNGP, J3DSys) via the Dolphin SDK's own
GDWriteXFIndx[ABCD]Cmd writers, so every caller was affected. Indexed loads were
broken for the entire life of this port.

1) Array selection had an operator-precedence error:

     GX_POS_MTX_ARRAY + (opcode - (CP_CMD_LOAD_INDX_A / 0x08))

   divides the CONSTANT (0x20 / 8 = 4), so INDX_A..D resolved to
   GX_POS_MTX_ARRAY + 28/36/44/52 -- far past GX_VA_MAX_ATTR, which is only 5
   beyond GX_POS_MTX_ARRAY. g_gxState.arrays[] was read out of bounds and the
   resulting garbage pointer faulted inside copy_xf_data
   (EXCEPTION_ACCESS_VIOLATION at 0x0).

2) The payload was misparsed. The authority is the SDK's own writer,
   dolphin/gd/GDBase.h GDWriteXFIndx[ABCD]Cmd:

     GDWrite_u8(GX_LOAD_INDX_x);
     GDWrite_u16(index);
     GDWrite_u16(((len - 1) << 12) | addr);

   -- a 4-byte payload. The parser read the index as a u8, took addrLen from
   payload+1 (straddling both fields, yielding addresses such as 0x0B32), and
   advanced 1 + 4 = 5 bytes, so every indexed load shifted the remainder of the
   FIFO by one byte and the parser eventually died on a bogus opcode.

Also adds a guard: an indexed load against an unbound array is a content or
ordering problem, so it is reported once and skipped rather than faulted on.

Verified field-for-field against the SDK writer. Nothing depended on the old
behaviour -- it faulted or desynced whenever it executed.

PROVENANCE OF THIS PATCH, stated because the extraction was not purely
mechanical: our tree carries debug instrumentation next to this code. Generated
with -U0 so adjacent probe hunks are not swept in, and ONE diagnostic call
(dump_anomaly, ours) was removed by hand from the guard. Everything else is
verbatim. Apply with `git apply --unidiff-zero`.

diff --git a/lib/gx/command_processor.cpp b/lib/gx/command_processor.cpp
index ef54b31..27cfa5e 100644
--- a/lib/gx/command_processor.cpp
+++ b/lib/gx/command_processor.cpp
@@ -419,5 +767,18 @@ void process(const u8* data, u32 size, bool bigEndian) {
-      u32 arrayType = GX_POS_MTX_ARRAY + (opcode - (CP_CMD_LOAD_INDX_A / 0x08));
-      u8 srcArrayIdx = data[pos++];
-      auto const& array = g_gxState.arrays[arrayType];
-      u8* srcData = ((u8*)array.data) + srcArrayIdx * array.stride;
-      u16 addrLen = read_u16(data + pos, bigEndian);
+      // The four LOAD_INDX opcodes are 8 apart (0x20/0x28/0x30/0x38) and map to
+      // the four indexed arrays in order. The operator precedence here was
+      // wrong: `opcode - (CP_CMD_LOAD_INDX_A / 0x08)` divides the CONSTANT, so
+      // INDX_A..D resolved to GX_POS_MTX_ARRAY + 28/36/44/52 -- far past
+      // GX_VA_MAX_ATTR (only 5 beyond GX_POS_MTX_ARRAY). g_gxState.arrays[]
+      // was then read out of bounds and the garbage `data` pointer faulted
+      // inside copy_xf_data (observed: EXCEPTION_ACCESS_VIOLATION at 0x0).
+      u32 arrayType = GX_POS_MTX_ARRAY + (opcode - CP_CMD_LOAD_INDX_A) / 0x08;
+      // Wire format, per the GD writer (GDBase.h GDWriteXFIndx[ABCD]Cmd):
+      //   u8 opcode | u16 index | u16 ((len-1) << 12 | addr)
+      // i.e. a 4-byte payload. This previously read the index as a u8, took
+      // addrLen from payload+1 (straddling the two fields, yielding garbage
+      // addresses such as 0x0B32), and then advanced 1 + 4 = 5 bytes -- so
+      // every indexed load also shifted the rest of the FIFO by one byte and
+      // the parser eventually died on a bogus opcode.
+      u16 srcArrayIdx = read_u16(data + pos, bigEndian);
+      u16 addrLen = read_u16(data + pos + 2, bigEndian);
+      pos += 4;
@@ -425,0 +787,13 @@ void process(const u8* data, u32 size, bool bigEndian) {
+      // An indexed load against an array that was never bound is a content/
+      // ordering bug, not something to die on: report it once and skip.
+      if (arrayType >= GX_VA_MAX_ATTR || g_gxState.arrays[arrayType].data == nullptr) {
+        static bool sWarned = false;
+        if (!sWarned) {
+          sWarned = true;
+          Log.warn("Indexed XF load with unbound array (opcode 0x{:02X}, arrayType={}, dstAddr=0x{:04X}) -- skipped",
+                   opcode, arrayType, dstAddr);
+        }
+        break;  // payload already consumed above
+      }
+      auto const& array = g_gxState.arrays[arrayType];
+      u8* srcData = ((u8*)array.data) + srcArrayIdx * array.stride;
